{
  "bug": {
    "bug_id": "Jsoup-27",
    "project": "Jsoup",
    "summary": "No title",
    "description": "In particular case a HTTP-Webpage responses with a invalid HTTP-Charset field (delivered UFT8 instead of UTF8).\n\nThis leads to an UnsupportedCharsetException in org.jsoup.helper.DataUtil at around Line 93(?) where :\n\nValidate\n.\nnotEmpty\n(\ncharsetName\n, \n\"Must set charset arg to character set of file to parse. Set to null to attempt to detect from HTML\"\n);\n\ndocData\n= \nCharset\n.\nforName\n(\ncharsetName\n).\ndecode\n(\nbyteData\n).\ntoString\n();\n\nI fixed it by wrapping a try catch statement around these two lines such that:\n\ntry\n{\n\nValidate\n.\nnotEmpty\n(\ncharsetName\n, \n\"Must set charset arg to character set of file to parse. Set to null to attempt to detect from HTML\"\n);\n\ndocData\n= \nCharset\n.\nforName\n(\ncharsetName\n).\ndecode\n(\nbyteData\n).\ntoString\n();\n} \ncatch\n(\nUnsupportedCharsetException\n\ne\n){\n\nreturn\n\nparseByteData\n(\nbyteData\n,(\nString\n)\nnull\n,\nbaseUri\n,\nparser\n);\n}\n\nIt now falls back to the none charset argument assigned clause, and tries to detect the character set via HTML."
  },
